WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.466
This lesson shows you how to clear website cache safely after an approved content change.

2
00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:10.126
Cache clearing does not save your work and does not correct wrong information.

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:17.891
We will save first, clear only the cache that applies, refresh the browser, and verify the exact public page on desktop and phone.

4
00:00:18.241 --> 00:00:22.267
An Editor may use an available record or page Clear Cache action.

5
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:27.099
Sitewide Breeze or Varnish controls may require an Administrator or Blue Nova.

6
00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:34.222
Never give someone Administrator access only to clear cache. Use only the control your role and instructions allow.

7
00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:41.482
Clear cache when WordPress confirms a correct saved change but the public page still shows older information.

8
00:00:41.482 --> 00:00:48.518
Do not clear cache before saving, and do not use cache clearing to fix incorrect text, images, dates, or links.

9
00:00:48.518 --> 00:00:51.243
First correct the content and save it once.

10
00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:58.464
Finish and review the approved change. Select Save, Update, or Publish one time and wait for confirmation.

11
00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:02.094
Copy or keep the exact public address that visitors use.

12
00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:08.770
You will use that same address for every verification step, without adding question marks or test text.

13
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.447
Return to the list containing the item you changed.

14
00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:17.665
Find the exact row and use its Clear Cache action when that action is available.

15
00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.470
This is the smallest and safest first step.

16
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:25.167
Do not clear unrelated pages, products, events, or practitioner records.

17
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:31.618
Open the exact public address. On Windows, press Control plus F five for one hard refresh.

18
00:01:31.618 --> 00:01:39.414
On a Mac, press Command, Shift, and R. Read the visible page and confirm whether the saved information now appears.

19
00:01:39.414 --> 00:01:41.719
Do not keep refreshing repeatedly.

20
00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:48.965
If the regular browser still looks old, open a private or Incognito window and paste the same exact public address.

21
00:01:48.965 --> 00:01:56.881
If the private window shows the correct result, the website is updated and the remaining issue is the regular browser's local cache.

22
00:01:56.881 --> 00:01:59.580
Do not add cache-busting text to the address.

23
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:09.275
Use the approved Breeze Purge All Cache control only when a saved change affects a shared page or several pages and the smaller cache clear was not enough.

24
00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:11.385
Select the purge one time and wait.

25
00:02:11.385 --> 00:02:16.631
Do not change Breeze settings, preload options, minification, or optimization controls.

26
00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:24.819
A Varnish purge may be needed when correct saved content remains stale after the applicable page and Breeze cache are cleared.

27
00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:29.361
Use only an approved purge control when you were specifically authorized.

28
00:02:29.361 --> 00:02:34.213
Do not open server settings, restart services, disable Varnish, or experiment.

29
00:02:34.213 --> 00:02:36.826
Ask Blue Nova when the control is missing.

30
00:02:37.176 --> 00:02:40.178
Do not repeatedly select Update or Publish.

31
00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:48.973
Do not purge object cache, Redis, a C D N, the database, image cache, or unrelated plugin caches unless Blue Nova directs you.

32
00:02:48.973 --> 00:02:53.091
Do not install, disable, or configure optimization plugins.

33
00:02:53.091 --> 00:02:58.327
Random purges can create a larger problem without fixing the original page.

34
00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:02.308
Open the exact public page with no extra address text.

35
00:03:02.308 --> 00:03:07.016
At desktop size, read the changed text, image, date, link, or listing.

36
00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:10.177
Click every public link affected by the change.

37
00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:15.153
Confirm that the page still fits the screen and nothing runs off the side.

38
00:03:15.503 --> 00:03:17.651
Repeat the same check at phone size.

39
00:03:17.651 --> 00:03:22.840
Confirm the changed information, images, buttons, and links remain readable and usable.

40
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:32.265
If the saved result is still wrong or missing after the approved cache steps, stop and contact Blue Nova instead of purging again or changing server settings.

41
00:03:32.615 --> 00:03:37.898
Every content change ends the same way. First, save the correct content once.

42
00:03:37.898 --> 00:03:40.642
Second, clear only the applicable cache.

43
00:03:40.642 --> 00:03:46.680
Third, open the exact public address and verify the visible result on desktop and phone.

44
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.796
If it is still wrong or missing, stop and contact Blue Nova.
